  "title": "The AI-native SDLC is paying off: 19% more PRs and 2–3 hours saved per developer per week",
  "summary": "Atlassian's analysis of 3,400 repositories across 2,500 customers reveals that teams adopting an AI-native software development lifecycle with Rovo Dev merge 19% more pull requests per month and save 2–3 hours of developer time per week. The article introduces a four-dimension measurement framework—speed, efficiency, quality, and satisfaction—for evaluating AI's real impact on developer productivity, and argues that engineering leaders should shift from tracking AI usage metrics to measuring productivity outcomes across the full SDLC: Plan, Orchestrate, Code, Review, and Operate.",
